      "title": "AI AGENTIC PENTEST FRAMEWORK IN THE WILD",
      "summary": "The report documents open-source AI agentic penetration testing frameworks, such as ARTEX, CyberStrike, PentAGI, Cairn, AntiFox and DesRed Team, that are exposed on the internet and increasingly used by threat actors. Researchers counted roughly 8,400 unique hosts across these frameworks, with the largest concentrations in the US and China and significant overlap with Cobalt Strike, Sliver, Havoc, Mythic and VShell infrastructure. Reported abuses include China-nexus groups such as Vapor Panda and Storm-0940, plus Cairn used autonomously to find and exploit a MONAI Label zero-day and to run mass web-attack campaigns. The report notes that many attacks still involved human operators in the loop, and that observed hosts may include honeypots. Defenders should expect these agents to automate reconnaissance and exploitation, making rapid patching of exposed flaws especially important.",
